      "side": 1,
      "message": "In addition to addressing your feedback, I made several changes in this patchset with a focus on simplicity and clarity, notably:\n\n- I removed the magic value from `--loops` indicating loop auto-tuning, and made that into its own `--autoTuneLoops` boolean flag.\n- I renamed some flags and rewrote their descriptions.\n- I added better flag validation.\n- I replaced `BenchmarkTarget::estimateNumRequiredLoops()` with `BenchmarkTarget::autoTuneLoops()`, and extracted the benchmark warmup behavior of `GaneshBenchmarkTarget::estimateNumRequiredLoops()` into a new virtual `warmUp()` method that must be implemented by all `BenchmarkTarget` subclasses.\n- I deleted some `BenchmarkTarget` methods that are no longer needed or that implemented behaviors that could be moved to `BazelBenchmarkRunner.cpp`.",
